Article 7
(1) Every Woman has the right to:
a. live peacefully, safely, in peace, happily, prosperously physically and spiritually,
b. live in a family within the bonds of a legal marriage;
c. maintain life and improve her standard of living;
d. have work that she likes and is also entitled to fair employment conditions;
e. obtain education and teaching in all types, levels and pathways of education in accordance with the requirements determined;
f. a healthy and clean environment;
g. receive fair wages in accordance with her work that is comparable and commensurate with human dignity,
h. elect and/or be elected in general elections, regional head elections, village head elections, village head elections and/or other political office elections based on equal rights through direct, general, free, secret, honest and fair voting according to applicable laws and regulations;
i. receive special protection;
j. receive special protection specifically in the implementation of her work or profession against matters that may threaten the safety and/or health related to women's reproductive function; and
k. special rights inherent to women due to their reproductive function are guaranteed and protected by law.
(2) Women who are adults and or are married have the right to perform legal acts independently unless otherwise determined by laws and regulations and other social norms.
(3) A legal marriage can only take place based on the free will of the woman and the man in accordance with laws and regulations.
(4) A wife during the marriage bond has the same rights and responsibilities as her husband over all matters relating to her married life, relations with her children and ownership rights and management of joint property.
(5) After the dissolution of her marriage a woman has the same rights and responsibilities as her former husband over all matters relating to her children, taking into account the best interests of the child.
(6) After the dissolution of marriage, a woman has the same rights as her former husband over all matters relating to joint property without reducing the rights of children, in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.
(7) Every woman who is in a condition of Disability, elderly age, and pregnant is entitled to receive facilities and special treatment.
(8) Every elderly woman, with physical and/or mental disabilities, has the right to receive care, education, training and special assistance at the expense of the regional government to ensure a decent life in accordance with human dignity.

